AIML (Artificial Intelligence Markup Language) is an XML specificationfor programming chat robots like ALICE using program B. The emphasisin the language design is minimalism. The simplicity of AIML makesit easy for non-programmers, especially those who already know HTML, to get started writing chat robots. One ambitious goal for AIML is that, if a number of people create their ownrobots, each with a unique area of expertise, program B can literally merge-sort them together into a Superbot, automatically omitting duplicate categories. We offer the both the source code and the ALICE content, in order to encourage others will "open source" their chat robots as well, to contribute to the Superbot. Botmasters are also of course free to copy protect private chat robots.
